# Swiss Steak (Flank Steak)

**Serves 6 | Prep 20 min | Cook 2 to 2½ hrs**

## Ingredients
- 2 to 2½ lb flank steak, cut crosswise into 6 portions
- ⅓ cup all-purpose flour
- 1 tsp salt
- ½ tsp black pepper
- 1 tsp paprika
- 2 tbsp oil
- 1 large onion, sliced
- 1 green bell pepper, sliced (optional)
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- 1 can (14.5 oz) diced tomatoes with juice
- 1 cup beef broth
- 2 tbsp tomato paste
- 1 tbsp Worcestershire sauce
- To serve: mashed potatoes

## Instructions
1. Preheat the oven to 325°F.
2. Mix the flour, salt, pepper, and paprika. Dredge each steak portion, pressing the flour in.
3. Heat the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Brown the steaks about 2 to 3 minutes per side and set aside.
4. Add the onion (and bell pepper if using) and cook 3 minutes. Add the garlic and cook 30 seconds.
5. Stir in the tomatoes, broth, tomato paste, and Worcestershire. Return the steaks to the pot and spoon the sauce over them.
6. Cover and bake for 2 to 2½ hours, until the steak is fork-tender.
7. Serve over mashed potatoes with plenty of sauce.

## Make-Ahead Tips
- Bake it fully, cool, and refrigerate in the same pot or in containers. The sauce thickens and flavors deepen overnight.
- Portion with sauce over each piece so the meat doesn't dry out when reheated.
- Freeze in individual or family-size containers.

## Defrosting & Food Safety
- Thaw raw flank steak in the fridge about 24 hours before cooking.
- Thaw frozen Swiss steak overnight in the fridge. Reheat covered in a 350°F oven for 30 to 35 minutes, or gently on the stovetop, until 165°F.
- Fridge 3 to 4 days; freezer 2 to 3 months.
